code: deny shell backgrounding idioms in bash/jobSpawn policy

The Bash tool's contract is "block until done, capture output". A
backgrounded child breaks that: it detaches from the call's pipes and
the model never sees its result. lofi.jobSpawn is the right surface
for that work (inspectable via jobStatus/jobRead, notifies on done).

Hard deny checked after tokenize and before extract_commands:

  - bare "&" anywhere in the stream ("&&" stays: sequencing, not detach)
  - nohup, setsid, disown as the first word of any segment
  - recurses into subshells and command substitution

Daemonising CLIs (docker run -d, systemctl start) pass through: they
re-parent work to a daemon, so the Bash PGID is empty at exit and the
contract holds.